# Evening MCQ — canvas: 20 Prelims + 15 flash facts

Ghost Recall stays **8 Q / 60 min** in the morning (chat is fine). Evening is one **canvas**, two tabs.

**New chat:** this file still applies. Do **not** ask Nik to retype answers or to re-state the flash rule. **Do not** start a paper unless he asks for one.

## Delivery (mandatory)

- One canvas, kebab-case, e.g. `evening-mcq-YYYY-MM-DD.canvas.tsx` in the workspace `canvases/` folder.
- **Tab 1 — Paper (20):** twenty Prelims-style MCQs. This is the real test. About **5 of the 20** are authentic CSE PYQs (labelled PYQ); the other **15** are from notes. Do not advertise it as “15+5” — it is one paper of **20**.
- **Tab 2 — Flash (15):** fact-recognition MCQs. Glance and click. **After** Tab 1, not instead of it.
- In chat, tell Nik to press **Open** on the **Canvas:** card at the **bottom of the chat**. Do **not** rely on a markdown file-path link.
- Do **not** paste 35 stems into the chat.

## Tab 1 — Paper (20) · ~45 min · scored

- **20** Prelims MCQs. One paper, one score: **+2 / −0.66**. Max **40**. Unattempted = 0.
- Inside those 20: **~15 from notes**, **~5 authentic UPSC CSE Prelims PYQs** (not a second paper).
- Four options (a–d). UPSC voice: “which is/are correct”, how many pairs, I/II, match, “with reference to”.
- **Not** a fact list. Each stem needs a trap (cousin, swap, class warning).
- Notes mix: ~8 today’s class · 2–3 due Mistake Bank · rest older notes (not tomorrow’s Ghost Recall dump).
- Stems from class + Yellow Book extras already on VR notes. Do not invent numbers.
- If time overruns, **shorten Tab 1 stems**. Never skip Tab 1 to do flash.

## Tab 2 — Flash (15) · 5 min · no marks · **same revision as the paper**

Canvas click-through stays cheap. **Do not** apply +2 / −0.66 to flash. Revision is **identical** to Tab 1.

- **15** one-line fact MCQs, four options, **recognition only** (date / name / pair / number already in notes).
- Source: **today’s classes + today’s Yellow Book extras** first; leftover slots from this week’s notes. Do not dump the whole bank.
- Clock: **5 minutes**. If he is still clicking, stop. Prelims skill lives on Tab 1.
- **Miss** = paper miss: Mistake Bank atom at **+1**, then the **same** revisit protocol (15-day while inside 90 days; 30-day after; a repeat bumps `Repeat Count` and resets to Day 1). Patch the cluster knowledge graph. **No extra Day-1 row.**
- **Hold** = paper hold: if that fact was an active MST, resolve it the same way (15-day next due). If it is a new class fact still on Ghost Recall Day-1, do **not** skip tomorrow’s Q1–Q2 — same as a paper hold on a fresh lecture.
- Same fact missed on paper **and** flash that night = **one** MST.

## PYQs (about 5 of the 20 on Tab 1)

1. Themes he **already has notes** for (`notes-index.json` + today’s classes).
2. Copy stem + options from `_pyq-index.json`. Label **PYQ** + `CSE-YYYY-Qnn`.
3. Check `_pyq-log.md`. Do **not** reuse an ID. Do **not** invent a PYQ. Years: **2016–2026**.
4. After he answers Tab 1: log the five IDs (theme, cluster, ✅/❌).
5. PYQ extra → `### Update — D Month YYYY (UPSC CSE Prelims YYYY)` on the original note. Patch that cluster. **No extra Day-1 row.**

## Scoring handshake (after Nik finishes)

Every evening / AWP MCQ canvas **must** have a **Send score** button at the **top** of the canvas and again at the **bottom** of Tab 1 (after the last stem). Do not ask him to paste `1-b, 2-a` in chat.

On click:
1. Reveal keys on the board.
2. Write a `scorecard` object into `useCanvasState` (sidecar `.canvas.data.json`).
3. `dispatch({ type: "newComposerChat", userPrompt })` with Tab 1 answers (`1-b, 2-a, …`), keys, misses (`picked x key y`), blanks, PYQ IDs, **and flash misses** (`F3 picked b key a (SOC)`), and: *Mark this attempt. Do not ask me to retype answers. Apply +2/−0.66 to Tab 1 only. Flash has no marks. Log PYQs. Paper and flash use the same Mistake Bank protocol (+1, then 15-day / 30-day / repeat reset). One MST if the same fact. A flash hold of an active MST is a paper hold.*

Put **Send score** at the top, at the bottom of Tab 1, **and** at the bottom of Tab 2 (so flash is in the sidecar when he clicks).

That click opens a **new** chat with the canvas @mentioned and the score already in the first message. Stay in that chat to log PYQs / Mistake Bank.

If he types **score** / **done** in the old chat instead: Read the sidecar `*.canvas.data.json` (`answers` + `flash` + `scorecard`). Do not ask him to retype.

Fallback only if both the prompt and the sidecar are empty: ask which numbers were wrong.

Agent computes **+2 / −0.66** for Tab 1 only. Flash Tab 2 has **no marks**. Log the five PYQ IDs. Missed **paper** items **and** missed **flash** items → Mistake Bank with the **same** gap as a paper miss (+1, then 15-day / 30-day / repeat reset). Same fact twice that night = one atom. A flash **hold** of an active MST is logged the same as a paper hold.

## Reveal colors (mandatory)

After **Send score** / flash reveal, do **not** paint pick and key the same blue.

- **Key** = `theme.diff.insertedLine` fill + `theme.category.green` border, label `· Key`.
- **Wrong pick** = `theme.diff.removedLine` fill + `theme.category.red` border, label `· Your pick`.
- **Correct pick** (pick = key) = green only, label `· Key (your pick)`.
- Before reveal, selected option may stay accent blue.

Copy this `McqList` option styling onto every new evening canvas. Do not invent hex.

## After Tab 1 and Tab 2

Treat every flash item like a paper item for revision (tracker + Mistake Bank + Next Due). Only the score is different.

Missed **paper** MCQ → Mistake Bank atom at +1, then 15-day (30-day after 90 days).
Missed **flash** MCQ → **same**. Do not also add a Day-1 cluster row.
